@page "/instructions"

<h2>Instructions</h2>

<h3>This page contains secrets about the application's work principles</h3>



<div class="notification-area">
    <div class="notification-bubble">
        <p class="notification-title">Single Prediction</p>
        <p class="notification-text">Enter the information in the order it is displayed on the screen. Hit the predict
            button to get a single prediction bsaed on your input data</p>
        </div>
        <div class="notification-bubble">
            <p class="notification-title">Batch Prediction</p>
            <p class="notification-text">Make sure you have a CSV file containing the data for a forest area. The order of
                the inputs matters, and is stated at the top of the page. When sure, upload the CSV and click predict</p>
            </div>
            <div class="notification-bubble">
                <p class="notification-title">History overview</p>
                <p class="notification-text">Every prediction made with your inputs is visible in your profile</p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="input-information">
            <h4>Input data format</h4>
            <p class="input-paragraph">The input information order for the CSV file MUST be as follows:
                <ul class="input-list">
                    <li>Elevation [meters]</li>
                    <li>Aspect [azimuth]</li>
                    <li>Slope [degrees] </li>
                    <li>Horizontal distance to hydrology [meters] </li>
                    <li>Vertical distance to hydrology [meters]</li>
                    <li>Horizontal distance to roadways [meters]</li>
                    <li>Hillshade at 9am (0-255) [index] </li>
                    <li>Hillshade at noon (0-255) [index] </li>
                    <li>Hillshade at 5pm (0-255) [index] </li>
                    <li>Horizontal distance to fire points [meters] </li>
                    <li>Wilderness area (1-4 in binary columns) [absence or presence]</li>
                    <li>Soil type(1-40 in binary columns) [absence or presence]</li>
                </ul>
                <h4>Result range</h4>
                <p class="result-paragraph">The possible results of prediction are as follows:
                    <ol class="cover-list">
                        <li>1: Spruce/Fir</li>
                        <li>2: Lodgepole Pine</li>
                        <li>3: Ponderosa Pine</li>
                        <li>4: Cottonwood/Willow </li>
                        <li>5: Aspen</li>
                        <li>6: Douglas-fir</li>
                        <li>7: Krummholz</li>

                    </ol>
                </p>
            </p>
        </div>

        <style>
            h2,
            h3,
            h4 {
                text-align: center;
                margin-top: 1%;
            }

            .notification-area {
                width: 90%;
                margin-left: auto;
                margin-right: auto;
                display: flex;
                justify-content: space-evenly;
            }

            .notification-bubble {
                width: 31%;
                border: 1px solid darkorange;
                padding: 0.5%;
                text-align: justify;
            }

            .notification-title {
                border-bottom: 1px solid orange;
            }

            .input-information {
                margin-left: auto;
                margin: auto;
                text-align: center;
                margin-top: 1%;
            }

            .input-list {
                list-style-type: circle;
            }

            .cover-list {
                text-align: center;
                width: 40%;
                margin-left: auto;
                margin-right: auto;
                list-style: none;
            }

            .cover-list li,
            .input-list li {
                border-left: 1px solid orange;
                border-right: 1px solid orange;

            }
        </style>